---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { name: 'About Us', href: '/about/' },
];
---

<Layout
  title={`About Us - Why We Built ${siteConfig.brand}`}
  description={`Learn about ${siteConfig.brand}: our mission to build fast, free, privacy-first image and file conversion tools that never upload your data.`}
  canonical={`${siteConfig.url}/about/`}
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-8">
    <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />

    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-4 tracking-tight">
      About {siteConfig.brand}
    </h1>
    <p class="text-base text-slate-600 mb-8 leading-relaxed">
      Learn all about {siteConfig.brand}: a digital utilities project by {siteConfig.company} focused on privacy, speed, and simple file conversions.
    </p>

    <div class="prose max-w-none text-slate-700 space-y-6 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Why Most Online Converters Are Risky</h2>
      <p>
        Most file converters make you upload files to remote servers. You wait in slow queues while their cloud processes your data. Then you download the file back.
      </p>
      <p>
        This old model creates real issues for users:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li>
          <strong>Privacy Concerns:</strong> Your photos, IDs, tax papers, and bills get saved on third-party disks. They can get leaked or shared.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Wasted Data & Time:</strong> Uploading big camera files uses up your mobile plan. It takes minutes to send and fetch the same data.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Annoying Paywalls:</strong> Old platforms limit how many files you can convert each hour. Some make you wait or ask for paid sign-ups.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">How ZixTool Runs in Your Browser</h2>
      <p>
        Modern web browsers are fast and capable. They come with tools like HTML5 Canvas and WebAssembly. We built {siteConfig.brand} to do all work directly on your own device.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you add an image, your browser loads it into memory. It decodes, resizes, and converts every pixel right on your computer or phone.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not run expensive backend servers. We only serve fast web pages. That is why our tools stay free, private, and unlimited for everyone.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Our Core Values</h2>
      <p>
        Every tool on {siteConfig.brand} follows four simple rules:
      </p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>Zero File Uploads:</strong> Your files never leave your web browser.</li>
        <li><strong>No Wait Queues:</strong> Your files are ready as soon as your device finishes.</li>
        <li><strong>Clear Results:</strong> You always see exact file sizes before you download.</li>
        <li><strong>Open & Easy to Verify:</strong> You can check your browser Network tab at any time.</li>
      </ol>

      <div class="mt-8 p-6 bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/90 rounded-2xl shadow-card">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Need to reach our engineering team?</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4">
          We welcome bug reports, format suggestions, and developer feedback from the community.
        </p>
        <a
          href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}
          class="inline-block px-5 py-2.5 bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-700 text-white text-sm font-semibold rounded-xl shadow-xs transition cursor-pointer"
        >
          Email {siteConfig.contactEmail}
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
